  "comments": "The real date is written in the stars on each side of the word &quot;UNA&quot;. An example shows 19 77 listed as 1975 77.<br />\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/54fb391d65d32.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/54fb391d65d32.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br /><br />\nThe 1978 issue was struck by three mints: Madrid Mint, Santiago de Chile Mint, and the British Royal Mint. They are distinguished by the style of script on obverse and position of numerals 78 on the reverse.<br /><br />\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/56157587ac72b.png\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/56157587ac72b.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"119\" /></a><br /><br />\n1978:<br />\n- above: Madrid Mint,<br />\n- mid: Santiago de Chile Mint,<br />\n- below: British Royal Mint.<br />\n(1200dpi scans from the actual coins)<br />\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/58a976b188eec.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/58a976b188eec.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"167\" height=\"250\" /></a>",
